From 2843ba7a646733977521c5ed43f81a6bff1f8f61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:11:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: Unlock with a fingerprint

When fprintd has a device and the user has enrolled fingers, keep the
device claimed while the lock screen is up and verify against any of
them; a match unlocks the session exactly like a correct passcode.
While a finger would unlock, the lock screen says so ("Touch the sensor
or slide up to unlock"). Hints fprintd reports while scanning (finger
not centered, too short, lift and retry) and unrecognised fingers show
up on both pages and wake the display, so a touch on the sensor with
the screen off either unlocks or explains why not. After five
unrecognised fingers only the passcode is accepted until the lock
screen is shown again.

The device is released when the lock screen goes away, however it
unlocks. Lock screens derived from PhoshLockscreen -- a greeter, say --
use their passcode for something else and don't get this.

This talks to fprintd over D-Bus rather than running pam_fprintd in a
second PAM transaction, as pam_fprintd cannot be cancelled once the
passcode wins, and it would keep the device claimed until it timed out.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
